+  // large EDRAM-sized framebuffer) are still limited by the guest viewport: primitives are
+  // clipped to it, so nothing outside is rasterized - don't load / store the rest of the
+  // attachments. (The host viewport can't be used - it covers the whole render target with
+  // the guest transform done in the vertex shader.)
